  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img height=\"251\" src=\"assets\\st0086_cbef0f5c6bbf.png\" width=\"798\" /></p><p>Terminal alkyne&nbsp;reacts sodamide to produce sodium salt of alkyne&nbsp;by elimination of ammonia molecule. Sodium salt of alkyne&nbsp;reacts with alkyl halide by&nbsp;nucleophilic substitution reaction mechanism. Secondary alcohol is oxidised by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to produce ketone.</p></blockquote>"
